hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27651","Haddathana Yazid ibn Harun, he said: Haddathana al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu Yazid, freedman of Abd Allah ibn al-Harith, from Umm Jundub al-Azdiyyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: O people, do not kill yourselves at the Jamrat al-Aqabah, and upon you be pebbles like those of khadhf."
"27652","Haddathana Hushaym, he said: Akhbarana Layth, from Abd Allah ibn Shaddad, from Umm Jundub al-Azdiyyah, that she heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, where he poured forth, saying: O people, upon you be calmness and dignity, and upon you be pebbles like those of khadhf."
"27653","Haddathana Sufyan, he said: O people, let none of you kill another; when you stone the Jamrah, stone it with pebbles like those of khadhf. My father said: And it was recited to him, Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas, from his mother, meaning from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
